## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical data quality, late data handling, and observability in a real-world lakehouse pipeline.

## Key Concepts
- Per-record contracts and simple validator logic
- Upserts into Iceberg star schema with deduplication by event_id
- Late data handling with watermarking (15 minutes)
- Lightweight observability: lineage, conforming vs non-conforming counts, metrics sink
- Trade-offs: Spark Structured Streaming vs Flink for beginner workloads

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo validator
function validate(record) {
  if (!record.event_id || !record.ts || !record.device_id) return false;
  if (typeof record.metrics?.value !== 'number') return false;
  return true;
}
```

